-## Edge cases
+### Edge cases
 
-- **Slots-file in unusual location** (e.g., `/tmp/foo.ndjson`): dispatcher writes `<slots-file>.output-files` regardless of directory; the orchestrator's own `$DESIGN_TMPDIR` placement of the slots-file means the paths-file lands in the same session tmpdir.
-- **Empty slot manifest**: now explicitly rejected by the new dispatcher guard (item 1). Paths-file is never written; downstream is never reached. Harness regression locks this in.
-- **Newline-bearing NDJSON `output` value**: explicitly rejected by the new CR/LF guard (item 1). Harness regression locks this in.
-- **Whitespace-only line in paths-file**: skipped by the `[[ "$path" =~ [^[:space:]] ]]` check in the new collector reader. If the file contains ONLY whitespace-only lines, the empty-entries guard fires.
-- **Failed slot in `phase3_failed`**: `final_outputs[idx]` still holds the phase3 output path (per the existing code at line 320); the paths-file includes it. The `collect-agent-results.sh` collector then reports STATUS=FAILED/EMPTY_OUTPUT/etc. — same as before.
-- **Whitespace in a reviewer output path**: should not occur in practice ($DESIGN_TMPDIR follows the `claude-design-larch6-XXXXXX` mktemp convention, no spaces). The new paths-file format (one path per line, no quoting) handles paths-with-spaces correctly via `while IFS= read -r path`; the line-oriented format also avoids the lossy `${final_outputs[*]-}` IFS-join hazard the `ALL_OUTPUT_FILES` stdout KV has.
-- **Concurrent dispatcher runs in same session**: impossible — `/design` enforces single-runner invariant (AGENTS.md); even if it weren't, distinct slots-files would produce distinct deterministic paths-files.
-- **Re-dispatch within same run** (e.g., dispatch-plan-voters retry path at line 167-186): the retry-waterfall call writes to its own slots-file-derived paths-file. The dispatcher's unconditional truncate-then-write guarantees no stale content survives. No collision with the original waterfall paths-file.
